# Milestone: v0.13.6 (Phase 0 harvest activation)
# Covers: e.syncEmit(p) — synchronous event emit; a SYNC-registered
#         (`at sync (e?)`) subscriber runs inline before syncEmit returns;
#         spec #3 §6.2 AT_EVENT_SYNC watcher mode.
# matrix-row: reactive-event
#
# Activation note: the original draft below used `at (e?)` (async-mode
# registration) and combined the emit and the read with `|` expecting the
# subscriber's write to already be visible.  Verified on this tree: an
# ASYNC-registered subscriber does NOT run inline under syncEmit (it still
# completes later, on the REPL's post-line drain) — only a SYNC-registered
# (`at sync (e?)`) subscriber does.  Same dot-syntax-vs-keyword-phrase class
# of fixture-authoring drift as Cluster #15 verdict A (see
# reactive/slot-change/slot_change_sync.chk); rewritten to the keyword form
# below, which is the form spec #3 §6.2 actually describes.  The placeholder's
# "not yet bound" blocker is otherwise stale — Event.new(), syncEmit(), and
# `at sync (e?)` are all live on this tree.

var e = Event.new()
Realm.order = ""
at sync (e?) Realm.order = Realm.order + "async"
e.syncEmit(1) | Realm.order
[00000001] <event>
[00000002] ""
[00000003] nil
[00000004] "async"
